cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this hardware accelerator design or verification suite in your research or educational work, please cite it as below."
title: "Programmable INT8 CNN Hardware Accelerator with 100 MHz Timing Closure on AMD Artix-7"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ATHENA Hardware Acceleration Project"
abstract: >-
  A synthesizable SystemVerilog INT8 CNN hardware accelerator featuring a 4x4
  weight-stationary systolic array, dual-port synchronous Block RAM ping-pong
  buffers, 4-stage post-processing pipeline, and AXI4-Lite host interface.
  Achieves 100.0 MHz static timing closure on AMD Artix-7 200T FPGA with full
  verification against a Python integer golden reference and RV32I SoC co-simulation.
keywords:
  - "CNN accelerator"
  - "systolic array"
  - "FPGA"
  - "SystemVerilog"
  - "Artix-7"
  - "INT8 quantization"
  - "RISC-V SoC"
license: MIT
version: 1.4.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
